# Everything here is excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# The first block is the reason this file exists. Without it, `docker build .` uploads the entire
# working directory to the daemon — including .env and production-secrets-backup.txt, which hold
# live credentials. Anything in the build context can be baked into a layer by a stray COPY, and
# layers are trivially inspectable in a published image. See docs/ENGINEERING_AUDIT.md MED-3.

# --- secrets: never in a build context, never in a layer ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*secrets*
*.pem
*.key

# --- build output: rebuilt inside the image, and stale copies cause confusing results ---
target/
bin/
!target/*.jar

# --- version control and CI ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# --- IDE and OS noise ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
*.iml
.DS_Store

# --- docs: not needed at runtime, and excluding them keeps the context small ---
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- local artefacts ---
*.log
eb-deploy-*/
eb-deploy-*.zip
eb-options.json
